# VEXARQ

The portable system lives in `.ai-vexarq/`. It evolves FRAMAI; do not delete the user-story workflow.

- Lifecycle entry point: `.ai-vexarq/workflows/lifecycle/orchestrator.xml`.
- Language: follow `.ai-vexarq/core/language.xml`. Detect the user's language. If the user names a language, use that language for generated code, text, and other artifacts.
- Default mode: `validar`. Use `continuo` only when the user asks for it.
- Write phase artifacts to `docs/vexarq/preliminary/`. The next phase reads only `docs/vexarq/current/`.
- Do not modify `.ai-vexarq/sources/canon/`.
- Do not push without a remote, a branch, and explicit authorization.
- Do not edit files outside the scope or break existing behavior to finish a task.
- When a lifecycle request ends, update `docs/vexarq/status.html` from the tracker template if it does not exist yet. Little text: phase, state, and link.
- A correction or a user story on existing code uses `.ai-vexarq/workflows/user-story-implementation/`, not the whole cycle.
